sn11.5:12.1 starts: You live for the good of both
sn11.5:12.2 starts: —your own, the other’s—
sn11.5:12.3 starts: when, knowing the other’s provoked,
sn11.5:12.4 starts: you mindfully grow calm.
sn11.5:13.1 starts: When you work the cure of both
sn11.5:13.2 starts: —your own, the other’s—
sn11.5:13.3 starts: those who think you a fool
sn11.5:13.4 starts: know nothing of Dhamma.’
sn11.14:6.1 starts: So conviction & virtue,
sn11.14:6.2 starts: confidence & Dhamma-vision
sn11.14:6.3 starts: should be cultivated by the intelligent,
sn11.14:6.4 starts: remembering the Buddhas’ teachings.’”
sn11.24:4.1 starts: “‘Bring your anger under control.
sn11.24:4.2 starts: Don’t let friendships decay.
sn11.24:4.3 starts: Don’t blame the blameless.
sn11.24:4.4 starts: Don’t speak divisively,
sn11.24:4.5 starts: for anger, like a mountain avalanche,
sn11.24:4.6 starts: crushes evil people.’”
sn21.6:2.1 starts: Swans, cranes, & peacocks,
sn21.6:2.2 starts: elephants & spotted antelope
sn21.6:2.3 starts: all fear the lion
sn21.6:2.4 starts: (though) in body there’s no comparison.
sn10.8:12.1 starts: The Buddha:
sn10.8:12.2 starts: the brahman totally unbound,
sn10.8:12.3 starts: who doesn’t adhere
sn10.8:12.4 starts: who’s without acquisitions
sn10.12:7.1 starts: The Buddha:
sn10.12:7.2 starts: —heedful, observant—
sn10.12:7.3 starts: one listening well
sn10.12:7.4 starts: gains discernment.
sn10.12:8.1 starts: Doing what’s fitting,
sn10.12:8.2 starts: one with initiative
sn10.12:8.3 starts: Through truth
sn10.12:8.4 starts: one attains honor.
sn10.12:8.5 starts: Giving
sn10.12:8.6 starts: binds friends to oneself.
sn10.12:9.1 starts: Endowed with these four qualities,
sn10.12:9.2 starts: —truth,
sn10.12:9.3 starts: a householder of conviction,
sn10.12:9.4 starts: on passing away, doesn’t grieve.
sn10.12:10.1 starts: Now, go ask others,
sn10.12:10.2 starts: common brahmans & contemplatives,
sn10.12:10.3 starts: if anything better than
sn10.12:10.4 starts: here can be found.”
sn11.3:16.1 starts: For those who have thus recalled
sn11.3:16.2 starts: Dhamma,
sn11.3:16.3 starts: there will be
sn11.3:16.4 starts: horripilation,
sn11.5:2.1 starts: ‘Fools would flare up even more
sn11.5:2.2 starts: if there were no constraints.
sn11.5:2.3 starts: Thus an enlightened one
sn11.5:2.4 starts: with a heavy stick.’
sn11.5:10.1 starts: They call that strength
sn11.5:10.2 starts: whoever’s strength
sn11.5:10.3 starts: There’s no reproach
sn11.5:10.4 starts: for one who is strong,
sn11.5:11.1 starts: You make things worse
sn11.5:11.2 starts: when you flare up
sn11.5:11.3 starts: Whoever doesn’t flare up
sn11.5:11.4 starts: wins a battle
sn11.15:3.1 starts: In village or wilds,
sn11.15:3.2 starts: valley, plateau:
sn11.15:3.3 starts: that place is delightful
sn11.15:3.4 starts: where arahants dwell.”
sn12.31:13.1 starts: Those here who have fathomed the Dhamma,
sn12.31:13.2 starts: those who are learners,
sn12.31:13.3 starts: When you, dear sir, astute,
sn12.31:13.4 starts: tell me their manner of life.”
sn15.10:7.1 starts: having wandered on
sn15.10:7.2 starts: then,
sn15.10:7.3 starts: with the ending of all fetters,
sn15.10:7.4 starts: he makes an end
sn21.3:6.1 starts: ‘As for Sāriputta:
sn21.3:6.2 starts: Any monk who has gone beyond,
sn21.3:6.3 starts: at best can only equal him
sn21.3:6.4 starts: in discernment, virtue, & calm.’”
